WEBVTT

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.360
My name is Albert Jexte. I am Latvian.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:59.330
I was responsible for all photography for the free Latvian government.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.740
The film you are about to see.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.370
is a true record.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.840
If the communists had caught me with it...

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.440
I would have been shot.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.770
This is this story.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.140
or what happened

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.130
to my country, Latvia.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.440
in one year.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.190
One terrible year.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.590
Then let we are.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.060
was invaded

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.280
and occupied by the...

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:23.830
Soviet

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.410
The scenes you will see.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.400
are part of history.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:29.600
they are

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.980
But I ask you.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.460
to look at them.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:34.800
and sing

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:36.720
Thank you.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:37.840
Latvia.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:38.900
happen.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.500
to other nations.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.020
Don't let it happen.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:43.820
York

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.060
Latvia is an ancient nation like Estonia and Lithuania.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.320
our neighbors on the Baltic Sea, which borders us on the north.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.620
On the south is Poland, on the west is Germany.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.820
and on the east is Russia.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.820
We Latvians have our own traditions, our own language.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:04.970
our own culture.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.630
Since the early 19th century, we have fought many battles for our independence.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.000
Our short history as a free nation shows that we have asked nothing of the world but peace.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.920
and the freedom to enjoy it.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.260
In 1918, Latvia won its independence.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.350
At the ceremony in Riga in 1920,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:40.000
Our first president, Chokster, is decorating some of the men who distinguished themselves

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.180
in the final struggle through which we won our independence from the Russians.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.810
National heroes were the men who helped to make us free.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.630
in honoring them as we are doing here in 1921.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.040
the entire Latvian people were voicing our determination to preserve

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.550
and make the most of the freedom we have won after so long.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.600
Something else happened in 1921.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:23.750
These are starving Russian peasants who fled across the borders into Latvia.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.740
They were among the world's first refugees from the Bolshevik regime.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:39.290
This is 1926, a great song festival in which our entire nation participated.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:52.220
Right, you see President Rylander of Finland, who was Latvia's guest.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.060
God bless Latvia is our national anthem.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:07.520
It was the closing song at this festival of a free people.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:18.920
In 1839, our beloved poet Virza wrote The Fateful Summer,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.840
prophesied the shape of things to come for the people of Latvia and the other Baltic countries.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.230
The summer, he said, will never again be the same as it was.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.970
The Soviet Union had demanded that we enter...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.860
into a mutual assistance pact with her.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.010
It was said that communist might

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.750
would protect the nations on the Baltic,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.100
but we knew that the treaty would be used

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.580
as a pretext for other things.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.930
October 1939, the borders of Latvia and Estonia

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:47.770
were forced open.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.030
The Baltic nations were to be hosts

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.850
to thousands of communist troops.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.460
In Latvia, they demanded these bases.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.500
These in Estonia and still others in Lithuania.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.750
On June 15, 1940, the town of Maslyanki was sacked.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.640
The Soviets claimed that we had attacked first.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:21.440
They told the world that a nation of 186 million people had to be protected from 6 million bombs.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.360
On June 16, we received an ultimatum.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.840
Submit to total occupation or be attacked.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:31.890
This meant the end of independence.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:37.940
June 17, 1940, they moved in to complete the occupation of all three Baltic countries.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.190
This was in direct violation of four treaties between Latvia and the Soviet Union.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:52.120
A peace treaty signed in 1920, a treaty of peace and friendship in 1921, a non-aggression pact in 1932, and the mutual assistance pact of October 1939.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.420
This pact guaranteed no interference in Latvian civil affairs.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.980
Against this armed strength, there was no possibility of resistance.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.440
On the same day, Andrei Vyshynski came to Riga to initiate the new order.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.180
He appointed a puppet government with August Kirstenstens as prime minister.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.670
Communists replaced every loyal Latvian in the cabinet.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.730
On June 21st, the jails were opened, supposedly for political prisoners.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.780
The men who were released were given uniforms and weapons.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.040
They became a new police force.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.400
On that day, the new government decreed a thanksgiving demonstration, and the people were ordered into the streets to participate.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.580
Special Soviet envoy Vyshinsky reviewed the parade from the Soviet embassy.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:44.750
He promised that Latvian independence would be respected.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.780
These are Russians who have been sent in as civilian technicians with the troops.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.930
The banners in science had been prepared by fifth columnists.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:58.990
These banners demanded that the Kierchenstein's government seek admittance into the Soviet Union.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:07.390
Johannes Spure, second secretary of the Communist Party, formally presented the demands to the Latvian parliament.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.830
Members of the parliament had also been appointed by Vyshynski.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.530
There were no opposing votes.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.180
Proceedings were watched carefully by members of the NKVD.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:25.490
On the same day in Estonia, an identical proposal was made before a new Estonian parliament,

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.700
with Soviet troops supporting the communist-appointed government.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.080
in the chamber was in direct violation of the Estonian constitution. On August 3rd,

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.950
Kierstenz left Riga with a delegation to the Supreme Soviet. As the head of the new Latvian

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:49.920
government, he was to petition for the acceptance of Latvia as a Soviet state. He was received

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.380
in Moscow with all the honors befitting his mission. Similar delegations from Estonia

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.540
and Lithuania would receive the same honors.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:07.150
This is the inside of the Kremlin. It has been very rarely photographed.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.530
The welcome for the Latvian delegation included applause from Stalin himself.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.000
Latvian delegation, led by Kierstenstein as prime minister, was made up of communists.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:24.270
They were surrendering the Latvian flag for the right to fly the hammer and sickle.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:34.590
He was made up of representatives of the other states in the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:42.800
He read his speech badly in Latvian. It had been written in Moscow, and he had not had a chance to study it.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:49.280
His audience did not understand it. They applauded on cue with machine-like precision when they heard the names of Soviet leaders.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:59.800
Other Soviet leaders besides Stalin were Kriushchev, Malenkov, and Zhdanov.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.860
On August 5, 1940, Latvia joined the Soviet Union. Estonia was next.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:12.500
Joining in the applause were Molotov, Nikoyan, and Gaganovich.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.210
An enthusiastic demonstration speeded Kirchensteins on his way home.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.110
There is little doubt that what had taken place was a triumph of communist planning.

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:29.070
For Kirchensteins welcomed back to Latvia Soviet troops with a guard of honor.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:40.380
red flag was flying over Latvia. It would also replace the flag of Estonia. Under the

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:44.500
new regime, national holidays were declared at frequent intervals, sometimes as often

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:49.260
as once a week. On these occasions, doors, factories, and offices were closed, and the

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:53.100
people were ordered into the streets for mass demonstrations. The theme was the promise

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:59.960
of the future, the dawning of a new era of peace and prosperity. There were two holidays

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:13.560
days a week. Latvia as a free nation had ceased to exist. Independent for exactly 22 years,

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:29.370
5 months, and 27 days. A new constitution was sent from Moscow.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:33.020
Kierenstein supported the Latvians to administer the new government.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:40.540
Yanis Asnis, 11 sentences for felonies, released from prison June 21st, became inspector of police.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:46.600
Yanis Pucinskis, professional thief serving three years and six months, chief of the Red Guard.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:55.600
Abram Zipe, housebreaker, serving a four-year sentence, became officer in charge of housing.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.490
Gutmannis, a felon serving three years and six months, appointed prefect of the second

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.270
police district.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:15.280
August Selmins, burglar, serving six years, he was appointed chief of police of Daugaufilts.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:22.860
Antis Botanicus, thief serving two years and one month, was appointed chief of police

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:23.760
of Leopaya.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:29.970
The new government appointed by the communists would govern according to...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.840
from Moscow. Those directives bore little resemblance to the Constitution.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.580
Communist propaganda machinery went into action immediately, reaching into

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:47.580
every aspect of our lives, telling us that we were still free and showing us

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:51.250
the benefits of citizenship in the Soviet Union. It was obvious that the

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.510
machinery had been set up and ready for a long time.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.560
movies made in Moscow replaced our own. There were a great many of them and it must have taken

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:11.940
months to prepare them. Radio Riga was taken over. The only news broadcasts we could receive

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:19.270
came from Moscow in Latvian. Every newspaper in the Baltic countries had its name changed. All

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:24.880
stories adhered strictly to the party line. Other sources of information were cut off. Our only

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.740
Latvian newspapers were put out either by Russians or by Latvian communists.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.780
books suddenly appeared in tremendous quantities and were followed by new poems and articles

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:41.720
supposedly written by well-known Latvian writers. Plays appeared too like this one presented for

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:47.380
our children. The character with a long nose symbolizes the spirit of childhood. He is

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:54.700
being given a map of the world. Garth is supposed to be a magic key that will give him control

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:59.780
over the entire world. The play to its juvenile audience was quite believable.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:18.350
There's a news story denying a rumor about nationalization

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:22.020
and promising that the rights of private property will be respected.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.960
This one, less than a week later, announced...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.000
is nationalization for the biggest banks and industries. What actually happened was that

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:39.900
everything was nationalized. All assets, other than purely personal belongings, were declared to

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:44.420
be the property of the state. And with the help of Moscow trained supervisors, everything was

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:49.870
inventoried down to the last nut and bolt. Business was at a standstill until the inventory was

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:59.020
complete. Personal bank accounts were confiscated. This woman was a domestic. During her entire

00:13:59.020 --> 00:13:59.900
lifetime she had

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:09.870
saved 4,000 lats. Under the new law, she was permitted to keep only 1,000. Workers were

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:15.380
ordered to voluntarily lend one month's pay to the state. In every factory, time was set

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:23.060
aside for the signing of pledges. Femmes were promised and carried out. Big farms were broken

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:27.830
up for distribution among the peasants. Each family received 10 hectares, which was not

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.980
enough to live on. In order to exist, the...

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:39.710
have to join collective farm papers they received were not deeds of legal ownership

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:47.430
herds were divided too the animals still belonged to the state technicians and farm equipment were

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:52.120
provided by the communists but as soon as the crops were ripe everything the communists could

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:58.700
lay their hands on was shipped to russia the new constitution guaranteed freedom from unreasonable

00:14:58.700 --> 00:14:59.100
arrest.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.280
But on one day, June 14, 1941, 14,000 men, women, and children were shipped to slave labor camps in Siberia.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:13.240
One of the first victims was Kaila Sulmanis, leader of the fight for independence and last president of Free Latvia.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:18.230
These death sentences were found in the pockets of corpses buried in unmarked graves.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.280
We found the graves after the communists left our country.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.800
This was the NKVD headquarters in Riga, vacated when the Nazis came in on July 1st, 1941.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.460
The cells in the basement were empty. The NKVD had left no prisoners.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:51.190
Next room was a torture chamber. Its walls were lined with rubber and it had its own drainage system.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:58.720
On this list are the names of 78 people. They were arrested by the NKVD on various pretexts.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:11.160
is the notation not politically reliable shoot them to death found their bodies and many others

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:16.400
in a mass grave in the courtyard of the rega city jail these murdered latvians were of many different

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:21.450
ages and from all walks of life there were government leaders and manual laborers some of

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:29.480
them had been communist fifth columnist i was there when many of the bodies were dug up

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.080
I helped to identify them.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:36.970
This was Colonel Lukens, aide to President Ulmanis.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.770
This was Pastor Uwe Zuelinj of Riga Lutheran Church.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.910
This was Chuiba, head of Latvia's high schools.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.100
This was one of the fifth columnists.

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:47.160
I can't remember his name.

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.980
This was Colonel Streba of the Latvian Army.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.380
This was Franz Kevich, a university student.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.070
I couldn't remember this one.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.040
this went on for months after the communists left as we found new mass graves in various

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:11.500
parts of the country we knew that there were others that we did not find altogether almost

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:26.100
15 000 bodies were recovered and reburied i was there on july 6th 1941 when this mass funeral

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:29.930
took place in forest cemetery outside riga i was at the side

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.100
the grave among the mortars as they listened to the words of Archbishop Greenberg's. These were

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:46.540
my people. This happened 14 years ago, but the memory is still fresh in our minds. My Latvia

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:55.120
is still occupied. After the brutal Nazi occupation, the communists returned. Those men Pashinsky,

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.840
Ryushchev, Malenkov.

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:05.000
Molotov, Mikoyan, Gaganovich and others are still in control.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:06.820
We know that nothing will be different.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:11.380
We cannot forget the 50,000 of our countrymen who were killed by the communists.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:13.800
You have seen what they did in my country.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.700
Don't let this happen to yours.
